        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Divisibility and Primes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This is EXACTLY what fails in Z[√-5]:\n  2 | (1+√-5)(1-√-5) = 6, but 2 ∤ (1+√-5) and 2 ∤ (1-√-5).\n  \"2\" is not prime in Z[√-5] in the sense of Euclid's lemma.\n  (It's irreducible but not prime — these coincide in PIDs, not in general.)\n```"
    },
